// @check
// @error-at 17:10 a `flat` type needs a record body
// @error-at 18:10 a `flat` type needs a record body
// @error-at 19:10 a `flat` type needs a record body
// `flat` needs a `{ … }` RECORD body (webcraft P1.2). A scalar alias, a union and
// an intersection do not have a layout, so there is nothing to measure.
//
// Reported at the PARSER, at the syntactic fork that decides the declaration form,
// because that is where the fact is — and that choice is why `UnionDecl` never
// needed a `flat` marker of its own: every non-record body parses as a
// `UnionDecl`, so rejecting at the fork means the marker never has to travel.
// Recovery is total: each declaration is then parsed as the ordinary non-flat
// alias it would otherwise be, so nothing cascades.
//
// These are PARSE diagnostics, which abort before the checker runs — which is why
// they live in their own file rather than beside the checker-tier shape rejects in
// `flat-shape-rejects.vl`. Inverted control: `flat-shape-rejects-control.vl`.
flat type Scalar = i32
flat type Union = { a: i32 } | { b: i32 }
flat type Isect = { a: i32 } & { b: i32 }
